1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,500
 This "cancel" button cost Adobe $75 million, but first, it cost you.

2
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:11,300
 Rewind to 2013. Adobe announces no new creative suite.

3
00:00:11,300 --> 00:00:18,600
 Software you bought once becomes a subscription. Subscriptions go from 11% of revenue to about 96% today.

4
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:22,600
 Here's the catch. The plan called "Annual" paid monthly.

5
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:28,200
 Sounds monthly. It's a one-year commitment. Quit in year one and you owe half of what's left.

6
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:32,500
 The FTC says it was buried in fine print or behind tiny hover icons.

7
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:36,700
 The DOJ sued in 2024, calling cancelling an obstacle course.

8
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:39,000
 In 2026, Adobe settled.

9
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:42,500
 $75 million in penalties. No admission of wrongdoing.

10
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:45,900
 But the unredacted complaint quotes one Adobe executive.

11
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:48,800
 The hidden fee is a bit like heroin for Adobe.

12
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:53,100
 Adobe says it wasn't an executive and the fee is under half a percent of revenue.

13
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:56,400
 Half a percent. Heroin. Same fee.

14
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:58,200
 And the fee? Not banned.

15
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:01,700
 Adobe just has to show it, math included, before you sign up.

16
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:04,200
 That cancel button? Still has a price tag.

17
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:06,240
 Every source is in the pinned comment.

